# The Zenodo concept DOI is added under `identifiers:` once the first GitHub
# release mints it. Version and date-released are finalised at release time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
title: "wgs-aggregate: cohort aggregation of per-sample WGS pipeline outputs"
abstract: >-
  A standalone Snakemake workflow that aggregates per-sample WGS pipeline outputs
  (sash, oncoanalyser, oncoanalyser DNA+RNA, DRAGEN) into cohort-level tables,
  builds per-pipeline report indices, and assembles the cohort germline genotype
  VCF. It is dataset-agnostic (the atlas, the consortium registry, or a future
  cohort) via a small deps/outs/params config contract, with no registry coupling:
  all sample identity comes from the dataset's consolidated samplesheets. It
  follows the lab "a stage is a product" pattern, runs standalone or as a git
  submodule within a DVC-tracked dataset, and is a faithful, behaviour-preserving
  extraction validated byte-identical to the prior per-module outputs.
type: software
